{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetOrder","@type":"LeanModule","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetOrder","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Basic","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgOps","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.CompositionLemma","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Flatness","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.WellFoundedSet","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Lex","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Prod.Lex"],"declarations":58,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.jet_stratified_correct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.jet_stratified_correct","kind":"theorem","line":465,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L465-L494","doc":"**Main theorem**: the jet-stratified + degree-bucketed algorithm\ncomputes the same normal forms as naive Buchberger, but with\nfewer S-polynomial checks and narrower per-step scanning.\n\nThe proof combines:\n- `jet_stratified_gs_criterion` (skip desc×desc S-polys)\n- `degree_filtered_reduction_correct` (narrow rule scanning)\n- `normal_form_unique` (result is the same either way)\n\nReference: [fred2005, §3] + [bergman1978, §5]. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:jet-stratified-reduction","label":"def:jet-stratified-reduction","md":"unital-groebner-bases/buchberger-and-pbw/jet-stratified-reduction.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.spolySavings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.spolySavings","kind":"def","line":461,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L461-L461","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.spolyCountStratified","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.spolyCountStratified","kind":"def","line":460,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L460-L460","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.spolyCountNaive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.spolyCountNaive","kind":"def","line":453,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L453-L459","doc":"**S-polynomial count** at level `n+1` under jet stratification.\n\nLet `m = |Σₙ|` (descended rules) and `k = |Σ^trans|` (transient).\n- Naive Buchberger: `(m + k) choose 2 ≈ O((m+k)²)` pairs\n- Jet-stratified:  `m·k + k choose 2 ≈ O(mk + k²)` pairs\n- Savings:         `m choose 2 ≈ O(m²)` pairs skipped ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetReductionConfig.desc_is_gs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetReductionConfig.desc_is_gs","kind":"theorem","line":451,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L451-L451","doc":"The descended subsystem is a GS basis (from previous level). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetReductionConfig.maxLMDegree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetReductionConfig.maxLMDegree","kind":"def","line":449,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L449-L449","doc":"Maximum degree of any leading monomial in the system. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetReductionConfig.system","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetReductionConfig.system","kind":"def","line":447,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L447-L447","doc":"Jet-stratified rewriting system. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetReductionConfig.jet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetReductionConfig.jet","kind":"def","line":445,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L445-L445","doc":"Jet configuration (level, generator counts). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetReductionConfig.ord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetReductionConfig.ord","kind":"def","line":443,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L443-L443","doc":"Admissible order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetReductionConfig.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetReductionConfig.mk","kind":"ctor","line":441,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L441-L441","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetReductionConfig","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetReductionConfig","kind":"structure","line":440,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L440-L451","doc":"Configuration for the combined algorithm. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.degree_filtered_reduction_collapses_type","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.degree_filtered_reduction_collapses_type","kind":"theorem","line":417,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L417-L436","doc":"**The deleted axiom collapsed `AlgElement G k` to a subsingleton.**\n\nStated as a hypothesis rather than proved outright, because the\naxiom is gone: this records what it *would* give.  Note it needs no\nwitness for `IsGrobnerShirshovBasis` or `ReducesToNF` — the two\napplications share one `nf_full`, so any inhabitant of the\nhypothesis suffices. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.bucketize","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.bucketize","kind":"def","line":368,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L368-L381","doc":"Partition a rewriting system into degree buckets.\n\nFor the Hecke algebra:\n- Bucket 2: Hecke relations `σᵢ² → …` and far-commutativity\n- Bucket 3: Yang–Baxter relations `σᵢσⱼσᵢ → …` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.DegreeBucket.rules","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.DegreeBucket.rules","kind":"def","line":366,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L366-L366","doc":"Rules whose leading monomial has this degree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.DegreeBucket.degree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.DegreeBucket.degree","kind":"def","line":364,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L364-L364","doc":"The degree (leading monomial length) for this bucket. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.DegreeBucket.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.DegreeBucket.mk","kind":"ctor","line":362,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L362-L362","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.DegreeBucket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.DegreeBucket","kind":"structure","line":358,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L358-L366","doc":"A **degree bucket** groups reduction rules by the length of\ntheir leading monomial.  During reduction, an element of\ndegree `d` need only be checked against rules in buckets\n`≤ d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.jet_stratified_gs_criterion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.jet_stratified_gs_criterion","kind":"axiom","line":324,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L324-L354","doc":"**Jet-stratified GS criterion** (axiom stub): the full system\nat level `n+1` is a GS basis if and only if:\n1. The descended subsystem is a GS basis (from level `n`), AND\n2. All desc×trans and trans×trans S-polynomials resolve to zero.\n\nCondition (1) is inherited.  Only condition (2) requires new\ncomputation: `O(|Σₙ| · k + k²)` S-poly checks instead of\n`O(|Σ_{n+1}|²)`.\n\nAxiomatised because the full proof requires showing that the\ndescended subsystem's GS property lifts through the inclusion\ninto the full system, using `descended_gs_inherited` plus the\nhypotheses on new S-polynomials.\n\nReference: [fred2005, §3], extended to jet towers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.descended_gs_inherited","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.descended_gs_inherited","kind":"axiom","line":301,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L301-L322","doc":"**Descended GS inheritance** (axiom stub): if the descended\nsubsystem is already a GS basis (verified at level `n`), then\nall descended × descended S-polynomials resolve to zero.\n\nThis is the key lemma that eliminates `O(|Σₙ|²)` checks.\n\nAxiomatised because the proof requires constructing the reduction\nof each descended S-polynomial within the full system, showing that\nthe extra transient rules do not interfere with the descended\nreduction (since transient leading monomials involve new generators\nthat cannot appear in descended monomials). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.classifySPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.classifySPoly","kind":"def","line":291,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L291-L297","doc":"Classify an S-polynomial pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.instReprSPolyClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.instReprSPolyClass","kind":"instance","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L289-L289","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.instReprSPolyClass.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.instReprSPolyClass.repr","kind":"def","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L289-L289","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.instDecidableEqSPolyClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.instDecidableEqSPolyClass","kind":"instance","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L289-L289","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SPolyClass.trans_trans","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SPolyClass.trans_trans","kind":"ctor","line":287,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L287-L288","doc":"Both transient: must check. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SPolyClass.desc_trans","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SPolyClass.desc_trans","kind":"ctor","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L285-L286","doc":"One descended, one transient: must check. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SPolyClass.desc_desc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SPolyClass.desc_desc","kind":"ctor","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L283-L284","doc":"Both rules descended: inherited from level `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SPolyClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SPolyClass","kind":"inductive","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L280-L289","doc":"Classification of an S-polynomial pair by the rule classes\nof its two constituent rules. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetStratifiedSystem.union_spec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetStratifiedSystem.union_spec","kind":"theorem","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L276-L276","doc":"The full system is the union of descended and transient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetStratifiedSystem.transientRules","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetStratifiedSystem.transientRules","kind":"def","line":274,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L274-L274","doc":"The transient rules (new at level `n+1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetStratifiedSystem.descended","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetStratifiedSystem.descended","kind":"def","line":272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L272-L272","doc":"The descended subsystem (inherited from level `n`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetStratifiedSystem.full","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetStratifiedSystem.full","kind":"def","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L270-L270","doc":"The full rewriting system at level `n+1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetStratifiedSystem.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetStratifiedSystem.mk","kind":"ctor","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L268-L268","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetStratifiedSystem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetStratifiedSystem","kind":"structure","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L265-L276","doc":"A **jet-stratified rewriting system** at level `n+1`:\nthe descended subsystem inherited from level `n`, plus\nthe transient rules introduced by jet prolongation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.classifyRule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.classifyRule","kind":"def","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L259-L263","doc":"Classify a reduction rule by examining its leading monomial.\nUses `jc.numGens` as the threshold: generators below it are\ndescended, those at or above are transient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.instReprRuleClass.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.instReprRuleClass.repr","kind":"def","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L257-L257","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.instReprRuleClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.instReprRuleClass","kind":"instance","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L257-L257","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.instDecidableEqRuleClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.instDecidableEqRuleClass","kind":"instance","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L257-L257","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.RuleClass.transient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.RuleClass.transient","kind":"ctor","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L256-L256","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.RuleClass.descended","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.RuleClass.descended","kind":"ctor","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L255-L255","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.RuleClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.RuleClass","kind":"inductive","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L246-L257","doc":"Classification of a reduction rule as descended or transient.\n\nA rule is **descended** if its leading monomial uses only\nlevel-`n` generators.  It is **transient** if the leading\nmonomial contains at least one new generator.\n\nThe descent involution `τ̂ₙ` projects transient rules to zero\nand fixes descended rules (vertex-algebra-jet-relations, D-1/D-2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.direct_limit_terminates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.direct_limit_terminates","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L231-L242","doc":"**Direct-limit termination**: for any element belonging to\nsome finite level `Aₙ`, GS reduction terminates.\n\nThe ordering `≺_∞ = ⋃ₙ ≺ₙ` is well-founded on elements of\nbounded generator index because `degLexNat` is well-founded\nand the bounded-alphabet restriction is a subrelation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.wellfounded_at_level","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.wellfounded_at_level","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L223-L229","doc":"**Well-foundedness at each level**: within the alphabet\n`{0, …, n-1}`, deg-lex has no infinite descending chains. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.ordering_extends","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.ordering_extends","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L203-L221","doc":"**Jet-embedding order compatibility.** The jet embedding sends each\nlevel-`n` generator to the *same* index among the first `numGens`\nindices at level `n+1`, so a **descended** monomial's ℕ-valued index\nlist is left unchanged by the embedding `φ` (`φ a = a`). A deg-lex\ncomparison of two descended monomials therefore carries over verbatim\nto their images.\n\nStated with the embedding `φ` and its fixed-point property on descended\nmonomials (`φ a = a`, `φ b = b`) as explicit hypotheses, and the\npreserved comparison **derived** by rewriting — not the old\nself-assuming `(hab : degLexNat a b) : degLexNat a b := hab`, which\nnamed the embedding nowhere and asserted nothing about it.\n\nReference: [leitner2026] §3/ordering-jet-compatibility. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.degLexNat_right_compat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.degLexNat_right_compat","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L172-L199","doc":"Deg-lex is compatible with right concatenation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.degLexNat_left_compat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.degLexNat_left_compat","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L153-L170","doc":"Deg-lex is compatible with left concatenation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.degLexNat_wf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.degLexNat_wf","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L136-L151","doc":"`degLexNat` (deg-lex, length-first) is well-founded. It has order type ω^ω — so it is not\norder-embeddable into ℕ, and *pure* lex is not well-founded (cf. the removed `lexLt_wf` in\n`NormalForms.lean`, where `[g₁] > [g₀,g₁] > …` descends forever). The length-first guard rescues\nit: `degLexNat = Prod.Lex (· < ·) (· < ·)` pulled back along `l ↦ (l.length, l)`, and the inner\n`(· < ·)` is well-founded on each length fiber (`fixedLength_lex_wf`), so\n`WellFounded.prod_lex_of_wellFoundedOn_fiber` applies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.fixedLength_lex_wf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.fixedLength_lex_wf","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L94-L133","doc":"Fixed-length lexicographic order on `List ℕ` is well-founded on each length fiber.\nBase case `{l | l.length = 0} = {[]}` is a singleton; the successor case is the head/tail\ndecomposition `Prod.Lex (· < ·) (· < ·)` via `prod_lex_of_wellFoundedOn_fiber`, with the tail\nfibers (length `k`) pulled back from the inductive hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.degLexNat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.degLexNat","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L88-L91","doc":"Deg-lex ordering on words over `ℕ`-indexed generators:\ncompare by length first, then lexicographically. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.monomialTransient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.monomialTransient","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L82-L84","doc":"A monomial is **transient** if at least one generator is new. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.monomialDescended","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.monomialDescended","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L78-L80","doc":"A monomial (word) is **descended** if all its generators are. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.isTransient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.isTransient","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L74-L76","doc":"A generator index is **transient** if it is new at level `n+1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.isDescended","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.isDescended","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L70-L72","doc":"A generator index is **descended** if it comes from level `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetConfig.totalGens","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetConfig.totalGens","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L61-L68","doc":"At level `n+1`, generators are drawn from a larger alphabet:\nthe original generators plus the new Kähler directions.\n\nWe model the extended alphabet as `Fin (numGens + numNewDirs)`:\nindices `< numGens` are descended (inherited from level `n`),\nindices `≥ numGens` are transient (new at level `n+1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetConfig.numNewDirs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetConfig.numNewDirs","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L59-L59","doc":"Number of new Ω¹ directions per prolongation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetConfig.numGens","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetConfig.numGens","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L57-L57","doc":"Number of generators at this level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetConfig.level","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetConfig.level","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L55-L55","doc":"Brane level index. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetConfig.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetConfig.mk","kind":"ctor","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetConfig","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.JetConfig","kind":"structure","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/JetOrder.lean#L48-L59","doc":"Configuration for one step of jet prolongation.\n\nAt level `n`, the algebra has `numGens` generators.  Jet\nprolongation `J¹(Aₙ) = Aₙ ⊗ Ω¹(Aₙ)` introduces `numNewDirs`\nnew Kähler directions (= 3 for SU(2)). ","signatureChunk":0}]}